diff --git a/wiki/sources/bekalu2025-black-cumin-heavy-metals-ethiopia.md b/wiki/sources/bekalu2025-black-cumin-heavy-metals-ethiopia.md
index bb57f1e4bbfbe6019f69740a1505d7b9340e3992..dc9df7ad46d0b7d757fa482d4dca657ace6567fc
--- a/wiki/sources/bekalu2025-black-cumin-heavy-metals-ethiopia.md
+++ b/wiki/sources/bekalu2025-black-cumin-heavy-metals-ethiopia.md
@@ -50,7 +50,7 @@
 
 ## Methods (brief)
 
-The study sampled Nigella sativa seeds from Dejen, Gozamen, and Sinan districts in East Gojjam, Ethiopia. Samples were subjected to microwave-assisted acid digestion and analyzed by flame atomic absorption spectrometry. Calibration standards for Fe, Cu, Zn, Pb, and Cd were prepared from 1 g/L reference solutions. Calibration linearity was reported as R2 above 0.998 for most analytes: Fe 0.9991, Cu 0.9982, Zn 0.9987, and Cd 0.9983; Pb was lower at 0.9889. Spike recoveries were 94.8-108% across the measured metals. The paper reports low LOD/LOQ values for Pb and Cd, including Cd LOD 0.045 mg/kg and LOQ 0.15 mg/kg.
+The study sampled Nigella sativa seeds from Dejen, Gozamen, and Sinan districts in East Gojjam, Ethiopia. Samples were subjected to microwave-assisted acid digestion and analyzed by flame atomic absorption spectrometry. Calibration standards for Fe, Cu, Zn, Pb, and Cd were prepared from 1 g/L reference solutions. Calibration R2 values were Fe 0.9991, Cu 0.9982, Zn 0.9987, Pb 0.9987, and Cd 0.9983. Spike recoveries were 94.8-108% across the measured metals. The paper reports low LOD/LOQ values for Pb and Cd, including Cd LOD 0.045 mg/kg and LOQ 0.15 mg/kg.
 
 The matrix is black cumin seed on a dry-weight basis. The measured toxic metals are total Pb and total Cd; no arsenic, mercury, chromium, tin, aluminum, uranium, or antimony values are measured.
 
